0 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242703 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242703 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242706 13194139533629 true] [17592186242703 1110 #uuid "adcdf2dc-f91f-5a27-b18e-901cd4c60f55" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242704 1034 "minutes per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242704 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242704 1111 #uuid "78f7cd9b-6556-5dfd-87cd-b363bf19c86d" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242705 1034 "hours" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242705 1111 #uuid "bdb9464f-e925-549e-8470-59faec1fc4ac" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242706 1034 "hours per minute" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242706 1111 #uuid "2b59a1b3-5ded-5da9-840f-8d94bd07652a" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242707 1034 "squared hours" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242707 1111 #uuid "688fab81-afa4-53d7-bdbf-9cb44efd4d75" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242708 1034 "minutes" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242708 1111 #uuid "c965b436-ff26-50e9-81d6-3260bf3ff6c9" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242710 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1089 "q-112091" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1100 "The function $S(t)$ gives the area, in squared centimeters, of a thin sheet of ice as it melts $t$ minutes after observations start. What is the best interpretation of ${S}^{′}(5)=-7?$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1113 #uuid "d99c466a-50e3-5f69-970e-e212baf18b71" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242709 1145 "The function ${S}^{′}(t)$ represents the rate at which the area of the sheet is decreasing $t$ minutes after the beginning of the observation.\n\nTherefore, since it is negative, ${S}^{′}(5)=-7$ means:\n\n$\\,$ *$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet decreases at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute.*" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242711 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242712 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242713 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242714 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242715 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242711 13194139533629 true] [17592186242710 1110 #uuid "7df7935b-2f86-5564-bd5f-d1d05a4e6f95" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242711 1034 "$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet decreases at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242711 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242711 1111 #uuid "864a91d3-feea-59f8-8d7f-040139534713" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242712 1034 "$5$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet is $7$ squared centimeters" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242712 1111 #uuid "8719c86f-60cc-5e58-a3c6-2112e0685dfc" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242713 1034 "$7$ minutes after the observations began, the area of the sheet is $5$ squared centimeters" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242713 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242713 1111 #uuid "cbc99222-4de4-530e-8be3-c2345a8f3e04" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242714 1034 "$7$ minutes after the observation began, the area of the sheet increases at a rate of $5$ squared centimeters per minute" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242714 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242714 1111 #uuid "eb2495b8-9e07-52fc-9742-82fb95d3b791" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242715 1034 "During the first $5$ minutes of the observations, the area has constantly decreased at a rate of $7$ squared centimeters per minute" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242715 1111 #uuid "9f73903f-8768-51e7-8b00-766cb2950911" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242717 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1089 "q-112381" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1100 "The decay rate $M$ of muons in a beam traveling at high speed can be modeled by the function $M(t)=2\\cdot {e}^{-2t},$ where $t$ is the time, in microseconds, since observations started. What will be the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds? Round your answer to three decimal places." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1113 #uuid "7487c467-8c5c-52ae-b53d-e72eead10381" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242716 1145 "The function $M(t)$ models the decay rate for the particles $t$ microseconds since observations started.\n\nThus, the decay rate of the muons after $0.5$ microseconds is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M(0.5) & =2\\cdot {e}^{-2(0.5)} \\\\  & =2\\cdot {e}^{-1} \\\\  & ≈0.736.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decay rate of the particles is $0.736$ muons per microsecond." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242718 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242719 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242720 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242721 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242722 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242718 13194139533629 true] [17592186242717 1110 #uuid "2f3adfba-33de-50ae-a048-a75334486e54" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242718 1034 "$0.736$ muons per microsecond" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242718 1111 #uuid "b6815bf6-c5f8-51a8-92c1-d4a939c88360" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242719 1034 "$0.346$ muons per microsecond" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242719 1111 #uuid "8b6fc2a1-6cb1-5bad-972f-1a7cef7b6c0c" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242720 1034 "$0.311$ muons per microsecond" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242720 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242720 1111 #uuid "3c645474-0ee1-5e40-8a2c-045be0f0c6de" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242721 1034 "$0.566$ muons per microsecond" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242721 1111 #uuid "ca761714-709e-5c96-82f7-01c36fc1aab8" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242722 1034 "$0.899$ muons per microsecond" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242722 1111 #uuid "87df36c0-7ca3-5514-9047-13ceda62b804" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242724 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1089 "q-112383" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1100 "After charging the battery of a PC, the percentage of charge decreases at a rate of $c(t)=100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2t}$ percent per hour, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the battery had completed its charge. What will be the rate of decrease after $5$ hours?" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1113 #uuid "7a8ec250-15a4-5b84-beef-886aee8058ea" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242723 1145 "Since we want to determine the rate of decrease in the amount of charge after $5$ hours, we have $t=5.$\n\nThus, the rate of decrease of the amount of charge after $5$ hours will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c(5) & =100\\cdot {5}^{-0.2(5)} \\\\  & =100\\cdot {5}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{100}{5} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of decrease will be $20$ percent per hour." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242725 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242726 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242727 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242728 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242729 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242727 13194139533629 true] [17592186242724 1110 #uuid "224f580d-b61d-5dc1-9b8b-cea24b724140" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242725 1034 "$4$ percent per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242725 1111 #uuid "80d0727c-d697-51f6-a221-b671f6b60ee5" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242726 1034 "$2$ percent per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242726 1111 #uuid "8f227591-2d70-5edc-b3a8-8d4e41fd1ba0" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242727 1034 "$20$ percent per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242727 1111 #uuid "78ed3e20-2e42-5b65-9e73-dd33c8efb962" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242728 1034 "$10$ percent per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242728 1111 #uuid "2a4d5967-cac6-5cb1-b155-8ef99342a97d" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242729 1034 "$40$ percent per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242729 1111 #uuid "46578e61-27e6-5678-b460-e7ff8dab9fb0" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242731 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1089 "q-112507" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1100 "The rate $O$ of the orders a car factory receives can be modeled as $O(t)=100t{e}^{-0.1t}$ cars per day. The rate at which cars are completed can be modeled as $C(t)=50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}t)$ cars per day. In both cases, $t$ is the time, in days, since the launch of the new model. \n\nWhat is the rate of change in the number of cars under construction $28$ days after the model's launch? Assume that an ordered car goes into construction as soon as the factory receives its order. Round your answer to the nearest integer." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1113 #uuid "ac818ad1-0395-53d8-9d76-66c7ed2e0c01" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242730 1145 "The rate of change of the number of cars under construction at time $t$ is equal to the order rate minus the completion rate, that is,\n\n$$\nO(t)-C(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $t=28,$ the rate of change in the number of cars under construction after $28$ days is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}O(t)-C(t) & =100(28){e}^{-0.1(28)}-(50+10sin⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{7}(28))) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50-10sin⁡(8\\pi ) \\\\  & =100(28){e}^{-2.8}-50 \\\\  & ≈120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change in the number of cars in construction after $28$ days is $120$ cars per day." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242732 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242733 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242734 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242735 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242736 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242732 13194139533629 true] [17592186242731 1110 #uuid "c06d622e-3b87-5d36-b691-d6ace7cf4eec" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242732 1034 "$120$ cars per day" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242732 1111 #uuid "b768dec3-61b6-50d3-91c6-fba939ea8138" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242733 1034 "$140$ cars per day" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242733 1111 #uuid "a16de123-27ad-566c-a3a7-01bdace48009" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242734 1034 "$100$ cars per day" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242734 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242734 1111 #uuid "ee17553b-b1d7-54b4-b1dc-91f74258533f" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242735 1034 "$125$ cars per day" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242735 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242735 1111 #uuid "0b3b2933-f9b2-5c2a-b258-cc5c785025b4" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242736 1034 "$162$ cars per day" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242736 1111 #uuid "c0698e01-e0db-5fec-9808-bbb3e13dd709" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242738 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1089 "q-112518" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1100 "Liam, a farmer, is monitoring the construction of a fence by recording the following two numbers for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in hours, since he started his observations:\n\n- $P(t)$ - the number of panels in the fence.\n\n- $r(t)$ - the rate at which the number of panels in the fence increases.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)?$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1113 #uuid "64fb28a9-2489-5d93-bbf0-bc7405527cc4" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242737 1145 "The function $P(t)$ gives the number of panels in the fence after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}P(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }P}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${P}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of panels increases at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $P(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${P}^{′}(t)=r(t).$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242739 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242740 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242741 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242742 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242743 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242739 13194139533629 true] [17592186242738 1110 #uuid "82476130-1441-5ecb-9866-4e1520954c05" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242739 1034 "{P}^{′}(t)=r(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242739 1111 #uuid "6e749ba7-2a95-53a1-beb1-c7ab58544a41" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242740 1034 "P(t)={r}^{′}(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242740 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242740 1111 #uuid "f99d5b65-75fc-5ec7-b3d7-d6f13be924c6" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242741 1034 "P(t)={r}^{2}(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242741 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242741 1111 #uuid "0280d6a3-b467-54c9-8024-31fec04a6152" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242742 1034 "{P}^{′}(t)=\\frac{1}{r(t)}" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242742 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242742 1111 #uuid "f0a7e8a3-2047-5cab-9a10-bf91c19b648f" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242743 1034 "{P}^{′}(t)=1-r(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242743 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242743 1111 #uuid "51b71153-c97e-54d7-bf25-9e57d03cf4ae" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242745 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1089 "q-112519" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1100 "To measure the number of children visiting a playground, Noah uses the following three functions that model the hourly number of visitors to the playground $t$ hours after the playground is opened to the public.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of children inside the playground\n\n- $E(t)$ - the rate at which children enter the playground\n\n- $L(t)$ - the rate at which children leave the playground\n\nWhat is the relationship between the functions above?" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1113 #uuid "d7e1b45c-7d22-59a8-850d-03ed8a91f836" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242744 1145 "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of children inside the park $t$ minutes after opening. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of children inside the playground changes $t$ hours after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of children inside the playground at time $t$ by finding the difference between the entry and exit rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t).\n$$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242746 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242747 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242748 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242749 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242750 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242746 13194139533629 true] [17592186242745 1110 #uuid "69c35e22-e8c0-507c-8873-0d6151eb8169" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242746 1034 "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)-L(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242746 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242746 1111 #uuid "0fd5d23b-7fd4-55e2-ab62-ded476aa5010" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242747 1034 "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)+L(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242747 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242747 1111 #uuid "296f76fd-6319-56a4-aa83-ebed27df183c" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242748 1034 "{N}^{′}(t)=E(t)\\cdot L(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242748 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242748 1111 #uuid "b072e35d-02a9-578c-8c7c-e555852d3444" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242749 1034 "N(t)=E(t)+L(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242749 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242749 1111 #uuid "bd387453-1f0c-5d5b-9d55-26a3241283eb" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242750 1034 "N(t)=E(t)-L(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242750 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242750 1111 #uuid "f4659473-5e7a-5d28-8400-3d980239e437" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242752 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1089 "q-112522" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1100 "Oliver, the owner of a platform for chess players, uses the following three functions to model the daily number of users of the platform $t$ days after it was launched.\n\n- $N(t)$ - the number of users with an account\n\n- $O(t)$ - the rate at which new users open an account\n\n- $C(t)$ - the rate at which users cancel their account\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1113 #uuid "73f18b8c-1751-5485-a092-111f7e091ec9" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242751 1145 "The function $N(t)$ gives the number of users $t$ days after the platform is set up. Then,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}N(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }N}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${N}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the number of users with an account changes $t$ days after opening.\n\nIn addition, we can compute the rate of change of the number of users at time $t$ by finding the difference between the open and cancel rates at time $t.$ That is,\n\n$$\n{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)-C(t).\n$$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242753 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242754 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242755 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242756 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242757 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242757 13194139533629 true] [17592186242752 1110 #uuid "acd7df3c-2bce-5ea3-88dc-2ed2ccb3ceef" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242753 1034 "{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)+C(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242753 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242753 1111 #uuid "413b05fa-e342-53be-a5f8-83ea32577a9c" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242754 1034 "N(t)=-O(t)-C(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242754 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242754 1111 #uuid "c089b227-d3c4-5ac7-9391-50815157d2b7" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242755 1034 "N(t)=O(t)+C(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242755 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242755 1111 #uuid "7f8d77fd-2943-5937-912b-45ff4b1cdf58" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242756 1034 "N(t)=O(t)-C(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242756 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242756 1111 #uuid "8c6cc255-9124-546e-b72f-4b07c8de0ac4" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242757 1034 "{N}^{′}(t)=O(t)-C(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242757 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242757 1111 #uuid "43dc12eb-2b95-5cba-b1ee-29e83088f68d" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242758 1034 "$4$ hours after the launch, the number of users decreased at a rate of $650$ users per hour" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242758 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533629 true] [17592186242758 1111 #uuid "81eea91d-8381-50e4-b2c5-9f8ccded11c6" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242760 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1089 "q-48611" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1100 "A cup of coffee sitting on a teacher's desk $t$ minutes after it has been made has the temperature $F(t)$ degrees Fahrenheit. What are the units of $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}?$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1113 #uuid "453a4f9f-dc2c-5ef4-9ab6-f86f7acd693b" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242759 1145 "We have that the temperature $F(t)$ is measured in degrees Fahrenheit and the time is measured in minutes. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t): & \\text{degrees Fahrenheit} \\\\ t: & \\text{minutes}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ measures a change in $F(t)$ over a change in $t.$ So, it represents a ratio of the units:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}: & \\frac{\\text{degrees Fahrenheit}}{\\text{minutes}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{\\text{d}F}{\\text{d}t}$ is measured in \"degrees Fahrenheit per minute\"." 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242761 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242762 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242763 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242764 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242765 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242760 1104 #edb/ref 175