194139533629 true] [17592186242837 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533629 true] [17592186242837 1100 "Douglas, a pilot, is flying a plane. The plane's control systems record two measurements for different values of $t,$ where $t$ is the time, in minutes, since take off. The two measurements are:\n\n- $A(t)$ - the altitude (height) of the plane\n\n- $r(t)$ the rate at which the altitude is increasing\n\nWhat is the relationship between $A(t)$ and $r(t)?$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242837 1113 #uuid "506715ad-75a6-5e80-881e-9c5f31214250" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242837 1138 false 13194139533629 true] [17592186242837 1145 "The function $A(t)$ gives the altitude of the plane after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\n{A}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}A(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }A}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, ${A}^{′}(t)$ gives the rate at which the altitude is increasing at time $t$, which is the same as $r(t).$ Therefore, the relationship between $A(t)$ and $r(t)$ is ${A}^{′}(t)=r(t).$" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242839 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242840 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242841 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242842 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242843 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1041 "selection" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242843 13194139533629 true] [17592186242838 1110 #uuid "4e91599e-df61-5bb8-93c0-39c95a687c88" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242839 1034 "A(t)=-{r}^{′}(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242839 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242839 1111 #uuid "b46f0f24-6d9e-549f-8848-f1663eacb939" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242840 1034 "A(t)=r(t)" 13194139533629 true] [17592186242840 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533629 true] [17592186242840 1111 #uuid 